{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the masters of arrows hated him.</b> Masters of evil tongue, as in: חֵץ שָׁחוּט לְשׁוֹנָם, \"their tongue is a sharpened arrow\" (Jeremiah 9:7). Among them was the chief butler, in saying: נַעַר עִבְרִי עֶבֶד, \"a Hebrew youth, a slave\" (Genesis 41:12). And among them were some of Pharaoh's servants who, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Sotah 36b), said to the king: \"A slave whom his master bought for twenty silver pieces — shall you set him over us?\""], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:25.643155618Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}